// Drive the PoS withdrawal path from a deploy, and report the result on a public name.
//
// `rho:rchain:pos!("withdraw", *deployerId, *ret)` only **stages** the request (law 47): it records
// the epoch-boundary deadline and changes nothing else, so the deployer's validator stays bonded and
// stays in the active set until that boundary — it keeps proposing. On a devnet the parameters are
// `epoch-length = 10000` and `quarantine-length = 50000`, so the boundary is far away and the
// validator is expected to keep producing blocks, which is the observable difference from a model
// that deactivates on request.
//
// Publish the `(Bool, Either)` result so `tools/devnet.sh query pos-withdraw` can read it back:
//
//   tools/devnet.sh deploy pos-withdraw.rho && tools/devnet.sh propose
//   tools/devnet.sh query pos-withdraw
new pos(`rho:rchain:pos`), deployerId(`rho:rchain:deployerId`), ret in {
  pos!("withdraw", *deployerId, *ret) |
  for (@result <- ret) {
    @"pos-withdraw"!(result)
  }
}
